TI  - Complementary and alternative medical therapies for attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder and autism.
AU  - Weber, Wendy
AU  - Newmark, Sanford
T2  - Pediatric clinics of North America
AB  - Complementary and alternative medical (CAM) therapies are commonly used by parents for their children who have attention deficit hyperactivity disorder  (ADHD) or autism spectrum disorders. The use of these therapies is well  documented, yet the evidence of the safety and efficacy of these treatments in  children is limited. This article describes the current evidence-based CAM  therapies for ADHD and autism, focusing on nutritional interventions; natural  health products, including essential fatty acids, vitamins, minerals, and other  health supplements; biofeedback; and reducing environmental toxins. The CAM  evidence in ADHD is addressed, as is the CAM literature in autism.
